Kubernetes Cluster
4

A Kubernetes cluster is a group of nodes that run containerized applications. 
It consists of a control plane (API server, scheduler, controller manager) and worker nodes that run pods. 
The control plane manages scheduling and orchestration, while nodes execute workloads.

Node

A node is a worker machine (VM or physical server) in a Kubernetes cluster that runs pods.
Each node contains kubelet, container runtime, and kube-proxy to manage networking and container execution.
